<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Couch: couchd's overlays over Plex (#18), the quick menu and the volume panel, as in the
  design's "Screen · Quick menu and toast" (sizes x1.5, like the launcher's ui/css/overlay.css).
  Toasts don't come here: couchd sends those as Kodi notifications (GUI.ShowNotification).

  service.couch turns what couchd sends (JSON-RPC JSONRPC.NotifyAll, sender "couch") into
  Window(home) properties:

    couch.menu = 1                     the quick menu is open
    couch.menu.title, couch.menu.focus  the app's name; the focused item's id
    couch.menu.<id>.label / .value     id: home, sound, volume, bluetooth, sleep
    couch.menu.<id>.detail / .hint     Sleep's "TV off at 21:20" and "OK: Off · 15 · …",
                                       drawn on its focused card; "" for the others
    couch.evening = 1                  deep colours (the evening palette)
    couch.volume = 1                   the volume panel is up (service.couch drops it after 2.4 s)
    couch.volume.name / .value / .step  the output, "60" or "Muted", the bar in steps of 5

  A dialog that opens and closes on its own visible condition, with nothing focusable: it
  never has focus, so Plex keeps every key. While the menu is open couchd keeps the remote's
  keys from Kodi itself and moves the focus here through couch.menu.focus.

  The volume bar is one image per step: Kodi can't size a control from a property.
  couch-*.png are white shapes, tinted here (system/kodi/make_art.py makes them).
-->
